# SPDX-License-Identifier: CC-BY-4.0
#
# Declarative structural assertions for the logic slice -- the slice-resident
# test-DSL twin of the asserted-TBox MUST / MUST-NOT invariants. Each assertion
# runs as a SPARQL ASK over the logic module graph (gmeow:scopeModule) under the
# native Rust slicetest harness (crates/slicetest). Sections 1-6 cover the typed
# context algebra; sections 7-11 cover the occurrent-refinement terms (the
# YAMATO/Galton process-not-equal-event distinction).

@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/examples/logic/tests/> .

# --- 1. The five typed accessibility relations are object properties (MUST) ---
ex:saTypedAccessibilityRelationsExist a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/>
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
ASK {
    logic:epistemicallyPossible  a owl:ObjectProperty .
    logic:doxasticallyAccessible a owl:ObjectProperty .
    logic:deonticallyIdeal       a owl:ObjectProperty .
    logic:temporallySucceeds     a owl:ObjectProperty .
    logic:counterfactuallyCloser a owl:ObjectProperty .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "The five typed accessibility relations MUST exist as owl:ObjectProperty -- each typed context kind reasons over its own named accessibility relation rather than one undifferentiated relation." .

# --- 2. No typed relation is rdfs:subPropertyOf accessibleFrom (MUST-NOT, keystone) ---
ex:saTypedRelationsNotSubpropertyAccessibleFrom a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:mustNot ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
ASK {
    ?r rdfs:subPropertyOf logic:accessibleFrom .
    FILTER (?r IN (
        logic:epistemicallyPossible, logic:doxasticallyAccessible,
        logic:deonticallyIdeal, logic:temporallySucceeds,
        logic:counterfactuallyCloser
    ))
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "No typed accessibility relation MUST be rdfs:subPropertyOf logic:accessibleFrom -- the generic superproperty licenses NO cross-type entailment by itself; an asserted subproperty edge would re-enable the cross-type subproperty inference the context algebra forbids (believed leaking into true, fiction into actual, ideal into is). The superproperty relationship is documented in prose only." .

# --- 3. No typed relation asserts an OWL property characteristic (MUST-NOT) ---
ex:saTypedRelationsAssertNoCharacteristics a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:mustNot ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/>
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
ASK {
    ?r a ?c .
    FILTER (?r IN (
        logic:epistemicallyPossible, logic:doxasticallyAccessible,
        logic:deonticallyIdeal, logic:temporallySucceeds,
        logic:counterfactuallyCloser
    ))
    FILTER (?c IN (
        owl:TransitiveProperty, owl:SymmetricProperty, owl:ReflexiveProperty,
        owl:IrreflexiveProperty, owl:FunctionalProperty,
        owl:InverseFunctionalProperty, owl:AsymmetricProperty
    ))
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "No logic: kernel accessibility relation MUST assert an OWL property characteristic -- the kernel documents logical character (strict order, non-reflexivity) in prose, matching logic:accessibleFrom which asserts none. The gmeow:sharpens characteristic (owl:TransitiveProperty) lives in the standpoint slice, an intentional asymmetry." .

# --- 4. PossibleWorld and Path are TBox classes (MUST) ------------------------
ex:saTypedContextKernelClasses a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/>
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
ASK {
    logic:PossibleWorld a owl:Class ; gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .
    logic:Path          a owl:Class ; gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "logic:PossibleWorld and logic:Path MUST be owl:Class with gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox -- the alethic-world and history kernel context types of the typed context algebra." .

# --- 5. ExecutionMode facet exists with both values and selector (MUST) -------
ex:saExecutionModeFacet a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/>
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
ASK {
    logic:ExecutionMode a owl:Class ; gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .
    logic:CommittedExecution a logic:ExecutionMode .
    logic:HypotheticalExecution a logic:ExecutionMode .
    logic:executionMode a owl:ObjectProperty .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "The execution-commitment facet MUST exist: logic:ExecutionMode (boxTBox class), its two values logic:CommittedExecution (default) and logic:HypotheticalExecution (the sandbox operator), and the selector logic:executionMode. The sandbox operator is realized as a facet value, orthogonal to the evolution facet." .

# --- 6. No reified modal-possibility operator class (MUST-NOT) ----------------
ex:saNoReifiedPossibilityClass a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:mustNot ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/>
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
ASK {
    { logic:Possibility a owl:Class } UNION { logic:ModalOperator a owl:Class }
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "No reified modal-possibility class MUST exist -- the sandbox operator (logic:HypotheticalExecution) is DISTINCT from modal possibility, which stays computed as the standard translation over the appropriate typed accessibility relation (logic:epistemicallyPossible / logic:doxasticallyAccessible) rather than reified. Conflating sandbox execution with modal possibility is the error this guards against." .

# --- 6b. Hypothetical-operator wiring terms exist (MUST) ----------------------
ex:saHypotheticalWiringTerms a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/>
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
ASK {
    logic:executedUnderContract a owl:ObjectProperty .
    logic:executedHypotheticallyAs a owl:DatatypeProperty .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "The hypothetical-operator wiring terms MUST exist: logic:executedUnderContract (the program-to-contract link by which the interpreter reads the execution-commitment facet) and logic:executedHypotheticallyAs (the content-addressed witness a hypothetical run records on its logic:TransactionOutcome). Without the link the contract-level logic:executionMode cannot select commit-versus-discard for a concrete run; the witness is what keeps the discarded run observable under suppression-never-erasure." .

# --- 6c. Concurrent-transaction (CTR) wiring terms exist (MUST) ---------------
ex:saConcurrentHistoryWiringTerms a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/>
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
ASK {
    logic:ConcurrentHistory a owl:Class .
    logic:precedes a owl:ObjectProperty .
    logic:serializabilityCriterion a owl:ObjectProperty .
    logic:concurrentComposedFrom a owl:ObjectProperty .
    logic:derivedHistory a owl:ObjectProperty .
    logic:violatedCriterion a owl:ObjectProperty .
    logic:anomalyCycle a owl:DatatypeProperty .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "The concurrent-transaction (CTR) surface MUST be declared: the native evaluator executes a logic:ConcurrentComposition and DERIVES a logic:ConcurrentHistory whose logic:precedes conflict edges (oriented by the witnessed interleaving), logic:serializabilityCriterion, logic:concurrentComposedFrom audit edges, and logic:derivedHistory link to the run's outcome carry the schedule; a cycle surfaces as a logic:SerializationAnomaly recording logic:violatedCriterion and logic:anomalyCycle. The serialization-anomaly engine consumes these terms, so they MUST exist with their declared rdf types -- a serialization anomaly stays a history-level finding, never a contradiction witness." .

# === Occurrent-refinement terms (YAMATO/Galton process-not-equal-event) =======

# --- 7. causalPartOf is a transitive object property (MUST hold) --------------
ex:saCausalPartOfTransitiveObjectProperty a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/>
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
ASK {
    logic:causalPartOf a owl:ObjectProperty , logic:transitiveProperty .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "Causal parthood among occurrents is transitive: a causal part of a causal part causally contributes to the whole. logic:causalPartOf MUST be an owl:ObjectProperty also typed logic:transitiveProperty." .

# --- 8. causalPartOf is NOT asymmetric (MUST-NOT hold) ------------------------
ex:saCausalPartOfNotAsymmetric a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:mustNot ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/>
ASK {
    logic:causalPartOf a logic:asymmetricProperty .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "Causal feedback loops are legal among occurrents, so causal parthood is deliberately NOT a strict order: logic:causalPartOf MUST NOT be typed logic:asymmetricProperty (contrast logic:properPartOf, the strict-order endurant parthood)." .

# --- 9. OccurrentBoundary has exactly the two members Open and Closed (MUST) --
ex:saOccurrentBoundaryMembers a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/>
ASK {
    logic:Open   a logic:OccurrentBoundary .
    logic:Closed a logic:OccurrentBoundary .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "The two-valued occurrent boundary: logic:Open (the on-going action) and logic:Closed (the completed event) MUST both be named individuals typed logic:OccurrentBoundary — the action(open)/event(closed) distinction carried as a closed value set." .

# --- 10. OccurrentConstraint members exist (MUST hold) ------------------------
ex:saOccurrentConstraintMembers a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/>
ASK {
    logic:OccurrentChangeAsymmetry  a logic:OccurrentConstraint .
    logic:OccurrentBoundaryMismatch a logic:OccurrentConstraint .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "The named occurrent well-formedness axioms a logic:violation may point at: logic:OccurrentChangeAsymmetry (a completed event cannot vary) and logic:OccurrentBoundaryMismatch (an occurrent cannot be both open and closed) MUST both be typed logic:OccurrentConstraint." .

# --- 11. occurrentConstituent: Event → Process (constitution, MUST hold) ------
ex:saOccurrentConstituentDomainRange a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/>
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
ASK {
    logic:occurrentConstituent a owl:ObjectProperty ;
        rdfs:domain logic:Event ;
        rdfs:range logic:Process .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "The constitutive reading of 'events are made of processes': logic:occurrentConstituent MUST be an owl:ObjectProperty with rdfs:domain logic:Event and rdfs:range logic:Process — the bridge from the unitary, completed event to the dissective process whose unfolding it bounds." .

# --- 12. CognitiveAssessment construct + projection + defeasible-evidence vocabulary (MUST) ---
ex:saCognitiveAssessmentVocabulary a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/>
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
ASK {
    logic:CognitiveAssessment a owl:Class .
    logic:AssessmentDimension a owl:Class .
    logic:SubjectGranularity a owl:Class .
    logic:AssessmentLevel a owl:Class .
    logic:LadderProjectionProfile a owl:Class .
    logic:DimensionThreshold a owl:Class .
    logic:DefeasibleEvidence a owl:Class .
    logic:defaultLadderProfile a logic:LadderProjectionProfile .
    logic:skillEvidenceForKnowsAbout a logic:DefeasibleEvidence .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "The canonical multidimensional logic:CognitiveAssessment construct, its value-vocabulary classes (AssessmentDimension / SubjectGranularity / AssessmentLevel), the ladder-projection profile machinery (LadderProjectionProfile / DimensionThreshold with the shipped logic:defaultLadderProfile), and the defeasible-evidence construct (DefeasibleEvidence with the shipped logic:skillEvidenceForKnowsAbout) MUST all be present -- they are the asserted-TBox spine of the cognitive-assessment layer (design/LOGIC-COGNITION.md)." .

# --- 13. The nine factored assessment dimensions exist (MUST) -----------------
ex:saAssessmentDimensionsExist a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/>
ASK {
    logic:dimensionAwareness a logic:AssessmentDimension .
    logic:dimensionDeclarativeFamiliarity a logic:AssessmentDimension .
    logic:dimensionConceptualUnderstanding a logic:AssessmentDimension .
    logic:dimensionProceduralCompetence a logic:AssessmentDimension .
    logic:dimensionTransfer a logic:AssessmentDimension .
    logic:dimensionExplanatoryAbility a logic:AssessmentDimension .
    logic:dimensionCalibration a logic:AssessmentDimension .
    logic:dimensionMetacognition a logic:AssessmentDimension .
    logic:dimensionReliability a logic:AssessmentDimension .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "All nine logic:AssessmentDimension individuals MUST exist -- the eight factored dimensions (awareness, declarative familiarity, conceptual understanding, procedural competence, transfer, explanatory ability, calibration, metacognition) plus the separately-introduced reliability dimension. They are an open value vocabulary; an assessment names exactly one (design/LOGIC-COGNITION.md)." .

# === Teleology layer (goal expressions, evaluation, plans, decomposition) ======

# --- 14. Teleology reified-node classes exist as TBox classes (MUST) ----------
ex:saTeleologyNodeClasses a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/>
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
ASK {
    logic:GoalExpression a owl:Class ; gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .
    logic:GoalEvaluation a owl:Class ; gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .
    logic:Plan            a owl:Class ; gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .
    logic:AndDecomposition a owl:Class ; gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .
    logic:OrDecomposition  a owl:Class ; gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "The teleology reified-node classes MUST exist as owl:Class with gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox: logic:GoalExpression (the typed IR goal-structure term), logic:GoalEvaluation (the reified vantage-indexed evaluation), logic:Plan (the transaction program with a goal-expression success criterion), and the two decomposition grouping nodes logic:AndDecomposition / logic:OrDecomposition." .

# --- 15. GoalExpression exists as the structural-identity IR term (MUST) -------
ex:saGoalExpressionStructuralIdentity a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/>
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
PREFIX skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#>
ASK {
    logic:GoalExpression a owl:Class ;
        skos:definition ?d .
    FILTER (CONTAINS(STR(?d), "STRUCTURAL"))
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "logic:GoalExpression MUST be an owl:Class whose definition documents its STRUCTURAL identity (two expressions with the same node kind, operands, and bound situation type are the same term). Structural identity is an IR/engine property not expressible as a single triple, so the assertion pins the documented intent rather than the equality relation itself." .

# --- 16. ActionSchema is punned as both class and node-kind individual (MUST) --
ex:saActionSchemaPunned a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/>
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
ASK {
    logic:ActionSchema a owl:Class , owl:NamedIndividual , logic:NodeKind ;
        gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "logic:ActionSchema MUST be punned (OWL 2 DL metamodelling): simultaneously an owl:Class (whose instances are reusable action schemas), an owl:NamedIndividual, and a logic:NodeKind, carrying gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox. The IR node-kind and the class of reusable schemas are one IRI." .

# --- 17. The eight action-theory facets are object properties (MUST) ----------
ex:saActionTheoryFacets a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/>
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
ASK {
    logic:precondition            a owl:ObjectProperty .
    logic:effect                  a owl:ObjectProperty .
    logic:invariant               a owl:ObjectProperty .
    logic:capability              a owl:ObjectProperty .
    logic:nondeterministicOutcome a owl:ObjectProperty .
    logic:observation             a owl:ObjectProperty .
    logic:compensation            a owl:ObjectProperty .
    logic:actionResource          a owl:ObjectProperty .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "The eight action-theory facets MUST all exist as owl:ObjectProperty: precondition, effect, invariant, capability, nondeterministicOutcome, observation, compensation, actionResource — the structure of a logic:ActionSchema that means–end reasoning reads." .

# --- 18. Goal / occurrence link properties exist (MUST) -----------------------
ex:saGoalOccurrenceLinks a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/>
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
ASK {
    logic:hasGoalCondition   a owl:ObjectProperty .
    logic:planGoal           a owl:ObjectProperty .
    logic:instantiatesSchema a owl:ObjectProperty .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "The goal/occurrence link properties MUST exist as owl:ObjectProperty: logic:hasGoalCondition (gmeow:Goal -> logic:GoalExpression), logic:planGoal (logic:Plan -> gmeow:Goal), and logic:instantiatesSchema (gmeow:Event -> logic:ActionSchema)." .

# --- 19. The four goal-decomposition relations exist (MUST) -------------------
ex:saGoalDecompositionRelations a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/>
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
ASK {
    logic:refinesGoal   a owl:ObjectProperty .
    logic:contributesTo a owl:ObjectProperty .
    logic:necessaryFor  a owl:ObjectProperty .
    logic:sufficientFor a owl:ObjectProperty .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "The four goal-decomposition relations MUST exist as owl:ObjectProperty: refinesGoal, contributesTo, necessaryFor, sufficientFor — the satisfaction-dependency structure typed apart from the generic mereology spine." .

# --- 20. The six goal-conflict relations exist (MUST) -------------------------
ex:saGoalConflictRelations a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/>
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
ASK {
    logic:contradictoryGoal      a owl:ObjectProperty .
    logic:contraryGoal           a owl:ObjectProperty .
    logic:preventsGoal           a owl:ObjectProperty .
    logic:competesForResource    a owl:ObjectProperty .
    logic:temporallyIncompatible a owl:ObjectProperty .
    logic:deonticallyIncompatible a owl:ObjectProperty .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "The six goal-conflict relations MUST exist as owl:ObjectProperty: contradictoryGoal, contraryGoal, preventsGoal, competesForResource, temporallyIncompatible, deonticallyIncompatible — conflicts between independently-meaningful goals, each weaker than the constitutive gmeow:counterGoal." .

# --- 21. No conflict relation subProperties counterGoal or properPartOf (MUST-NOT)
ex:saConflictRelationsNotSubproperty a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:mustNot ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
ASK {
    ?r rdfs:subPropertyOf ?super .
    FILTER (?r IN (
        logic:contradictoryGoal, logic:contraryGoal, logic:preventsGoal,
        logic:competesForResource, logic:temporallyIncompatible,
        logic:deonticallyIncompatible
    ))
    FILTER (?super IN (gmeow:counterGoal, gmeow:properPartOf))
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "No logic: goal-conflict relation MUST be rdfs:subPropertyOf gmeow:counterGoal (the strongest, constitutive opposition) or gmeow:properPartOf (structural part-hood) — the six are ordinary relations between independently-meaningful goals, weaker than counterGoal and orthogonal to mereology; a subproperty edge would manufacture exactly the conflation this guards against." .

# --- 22. The four factored GoalEvaluation status classes exist (MUST) --------
ex:saGoalEvaluationStatusClasses a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/>
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
ASK {
    logic:SatisfactionStatus   a owl:Class ; gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .
    logic:FeasibilityStatus    a owl:Class ; gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .
    logic:LifecycleStatus      a owl:Class ; gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .
    logic:GoalEvaluationStatus a owl:Class ; gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .
    logic:Satisfied      a logic:SatisfactionStatus .
    logic:Feasible       a logic:FeasibilityStatus .
    logic:LifecycleActive a logic:LifecycleStatus .
    logic:GoalEvaluationCompleted a logic:GoalEvaluationStatus .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "The four factored goal-evaluation status value classes MUST exist as boxTBox owl:Class with representative members: logic:SatisfactionStatus, logic:FeasibilityStatus, logic:LifecycleStatus, and logic:GoalEvaluationStatus — independent axes of a logic:GoalEvaluation rather than one collapsed label." .

# --- 23. GoalEvaluationStatus is DISTINCT from EvaluationStatus (MUST) --------
ex:saGoalEvaluationStatusDistinct a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/>
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
ASK {
    logic:GoalEvaluationStatus a owl:Class .
    logic:EvaluationStatus     a owl:Class .
    FILTER (logic:GoalEvaluationStatus != logic:EvaluationStatus)
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "logic:GoalEvaluationStatus (the goal-judgment conclusiveness axis) MUST be a DISTINCT owl:Class from logic:EvaluationStatus (the engine-computation axis of a logic:ReasoningResult) — two orthogonal axes that must never be conflated into one value set." .

# --- 24. GoalEvaluation axis + quantity + link properties exist (MUST) --------
ex:saGoalEvaluationProperties a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/>
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
ASK {
    logic:satisfactionStatus   a owl:ObjectProperty .
    logic:feasibilityStatus    a owl:ObjectProperty .
    logic:lifecycleStatus      a owl:ObjectProperty .
    logic:goalEvaluationStatus a owl:ObjectProperty .
    logic:evaluatesGoal        a owl:ObjectProperty .
    logic:evaluatedAgainst     a owl:ObjectProperty .
    logic:evaluationCriterion  a owl:ObjectProperty .
    logic:evaluationEvaluator  a owl:ObjectProperty .
    logic:objectiveDirection   a owl:ObjectProperty .
    logic:satisfactionDegree   a owl:DatatypeProperty .
    logic:objectiveValue       a owl:DatatypeProperty .
    logic:utility              a owl:DatatypeProperty .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "The goal-evaluation axis selectors (satisfactionStatus, feasibilityStatus, lifecycleStatus, goalEvaluationStatus), links (evaluatesGoal, evaluatedAgainst, evaluationCriterion, evaluationEvaluator), and quantities MUST exist — the three unit-interval quantities (satisfactionDegree, objectiveValue, utility) as owl:DatatypeProperty matching the logic:confidence/logic:weight idiom, the rest as owl:ObjectProperty." .

# --- 25. Plan success quantification exists as a closed value set (MUST) ------
ex:saPlanSuccessMode a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/>
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
ASK {
    logic:PlanSuccessMode a owl:Class ; gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .
    logic:WeakPlanSuccess        a logic:PlanSuccessMode .
    logic:StrongPlanSuccess      a logic:PlanSuccessMode .
    logic:StrongCyclicPlanSuccess a logic:PlanSuccessMode .
    logic:planSuccessMode a owl:ObjectProperty .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "Plan success MUST be quantified over nondeterministic outcomes as a closed value set: logic:PlanSuccessMode (boxTBox class) with its three members logic:WeakPlanSuccess (some path), logic:StrongPlanSuccess (every path), logic:StrongCyclicPlanSuccess (every fair execution), plus the selector logic:planSuccessMode (logic:Plan -> logic:PlanSuccessMode)." .

# --- 26. Transaction-layer new classes + supersededBy property exist (MUST) ---
ex:saTransactionLayerClassesExist a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/>
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
ASK {
    logic:SerialConjunction          a owl:Class .
    logic:SerializabilityCriterion   a owl:Class .
    logic:IsolationLevel             a owl:Class .
    logic:ConcurrencyControlProtocol a owl:Class .
    logic:SerializationAnomaly       a owl:Class .
    logic:supersededBy               a owl:ObjectProperty .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "The transaction-layer additions MUST exist with their correct rdf:type: the five new classes (SerialConjunction, the three concurrency value-set classes, SerializationAnomaly) as owl:Class, and the supersession-provenance counterpart logic:supersededBy as owl:ObjectProperty (the fourth provenance link that makes every del a supersession)." .

# --- 27. Serial-conjunction combinator carries its two operands (MUST) --------
ex:saSerialConjunctionOperands a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/>
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
ASK {
    logic:SerialConjunction a owl:Class ; gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .
    logic:leftOperand  a owl:ObjectProperty .
    logic:rightOperand a owl:ObjectProperty .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "The serial-conjunction program combinator (a boxTBox class) MUST carry its binary operands logic:leftOperand and logic:rightOperand as object properties -- it is a program operator typed apart from logical conjunction." .

# --- 28. Plan-to-path link exists (MUST) -------------------------------------
ex:saPlanExecutedAlongPath a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/>
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
ASK {
    logic:executedAlongPath a owl:ObjectProperty .
    logic:Plan a owl:Class .
    logic:Path a owl:Class .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "The four-link chain intention -> plan -> action -> transaction-path MUST be completed by logic:executedAlongPath relating a logic:Plan to the logic:Path it ran along -- the one link existing terms did not supply; it connects but does not subsume the two." .

# --- 29. The three concurrency value-set classes are pairwise distinct IRIs (MUST) ---
ex:saConcurrencyConcernsAreDistinct a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/>
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
ASK {
    logic:SerializabilityCriterion   a owl:Class .
    logic:IsolationLevel             a owl:Class .
    logic:ConcurrencyControlProtocol a owl:Class .
    FILTER (logic:SerializabilityCriterion != logic:IsolationLevel)
    FILTER (logic:SerializabilityCriterion != logic:ConcurrencyControlProtocol)
    FILTER (logic:IsolationLevel != logic:ConcurrencyControlProtocol)
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "The three concurrency concerns MUST be three distinct, separately-declared owl:Class IRIs that are never conflated: a criterion is a history property, a level is a guarantee strength, a protocol is a mechanism." .

# --- 30. The three concurrency value sets enumerate the right members (MUST) --
ex:saConcurrencyValueSetMembers a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/>
ASK {
    logic:ConflictSerializability a logic:SerializabilityCriterion .
    logic:ViewSerializability     a logic:SerializabilityCriterion .
    logic:ReadUncommittedIsolation a logic:IsolationLevel .
    logic:ReadCommittedIsolation   a logic:IsolationLevel .
    logic:RepeatableReadIsolation  a logic:IsolationLevel .
    logic:SnapshotIsolation        a logic:IsolationLevel .
    logic:SerializableIsolation    a logic:IsolationLevel .
    logic:OpacityIsolation         a logic:IsolationLevel .
    logic:StrictTwoPhaseLocking       a logic:ConcurrencyControlProtocol .
    logic:StrongStrictTwoPhaseLocking a logic:ConcurrencyControlProtocol .
    logic:TimestampOrdering           a logic:ConcurrencyControlProtocol .
    logic:OptimisticValidation        a logic:ConcurrencyControlProtocol .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "Each of the three closed concurrency value sets MUST enumerate exactly its declared members: the two serializability criteria, the six isolation levels (through opacity), and the four concurrency-control protocols." .

# --- 31. SerializationAnomaly is NOT a contradiction witness (MUST) -----------
# There is no canonical contradiction-WITNESS CLASS in the module: the witness is
# carried by the property logic:contradictionWitness and the verdict value
# logic:InfoBoth. So the not-a-contradiction intent is pinned in TEXT: the class
# exists with a definition CONTAINING the word "finding".
ex:saSerializationAnomalyIsAFinding a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/>
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
PREFIX skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#>
ASK {
    logic:SerializationAnomaly a owl:Class ;
        skos:definition ?d .
    FILTER (CONTAINS(STR(?d), "finding"))
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "logic:SerializationAnomaly MUST be a history-level finding, NOT a contradiction witness. There is no single canonical contradiction-witness CLASS (the witness is the property logic:contradictionWitness / the verdict logic:InfoBoth), so the not-a-contradiction intent is pinned in text: the class definition MUST contain the word 'finding', distinguishing it from a contradiction witness that asserts a logical contradiction within a state." .

# === Engine representation vocabulary ========================================
# The goal-expression structure, per-outcome compensation reification, and the
# situation-obtains reading the native teleology evaluator (crates/logic/src/
# teleology.rs) reads and emits. Normative in design/LOGIC-TELEOLOGY.md.

# --- GoalExpressionKind is a closed nine-member value set (MUST) --------------
ex:saGoalExpressionKindClosedSet a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/>
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
ASK {
    logic:GoalExpressionKind a owl:Class ; gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .
    logic:AtomicGoal         a logic:GoalExpressionKind .
    logic:ConjunctiveGoal    a logic:GoalExpressionKind .
    logic:DisjunctiveGoal    a logic:GoalExpressionKind .
    logic:AchievementGoal    a logic:GoalExpressionKind .
    logic:MaintenanceGoal    a logic:GoalExpressionKind .
    logic:AvoidanceGoal      a logic:GoalExpressionKind .
    logic:OptimizationGoal   a logic:GoalExpressionKind .
    logic:ConditionalGoal    a logic:GoalExpressionKind .
    logic:DeadlineWindowGoal a logic:GoalExpressionKind .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "logic:GoalExpressionKind MUST be a boxTBox owl:Class whose closed value set is exactly the nine compositional variants the engine dispatches on: AtomicGoal, ConjunctiveGoal, DisjunctiveGoal, AchievementGoal, MaintenanceGoal, AvoidanceGoal, OptimizationGoal, ConditionalGoal, DeadlineWindowGoal." .

# --- Goal-expression structure properties exist (MUST) -----------------------
ex:saGoalExpressionStructureProps a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/>
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
ASK {
    logic:goalExpressionKind a owl:ObjectProperty .
    logic:operand            a owl:ObjectProperty .
    logic:boundSituationType a owl:ObjectProperty .
    logic:guardSituation     a owl:ObjectProperty .
    logic:deadlineWindow     a owl:ObjectProperty .
    logic:situationObtains   a owl:ObjectProperty .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "The goal-expression structure the engine reads MUST exist as owl:ObjectProperty: logic:goalExpressionKind (selects the variant), logic:operand (sub-expressions of a conjunctive/disjunctive/conditional/deadline goal), logic:boundSituationType (the targeted situation type), logic:guardSituation (a conditional goal's guard), logic:deadlineWindow (a deadline-window goal's bounding interval), and logic:situationObtains (a situation type holds at a state)." .

# --- Outcome reifies a branch with its own compensation (MUST) ---------------
ex:saOutcomePerBranchCompensation a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/>
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
ASK {
    logic:Outcome          a owl:Class ; gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .
    logic:outcomeSituation a owl:ObjectProperty .
    logic:compensation     a owl:ObjectProperty .
    logic:nondeterministicOutcome a owl:ObjectProperty .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "A nondeterministic branch MUST be reified: logic:Outcome (boxTBox owl:Class) carries via logic:outcomeSituation the successor it reaches and reuses logic:compensation so each branch names the recovery for IT specifically; logic:nondeterministicOutcome points a logic:ActionSchema at its logic:Outcome branches, so compensation is outcome-indexed rather than one generic undo." .

# --- GoalEvaluationUndetermined is the open-window value (MUST) ---------------
ex:saGoalEvaluationUndeterminedExists a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/>
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
ASK {
    logic:GoalEvaluationUndetermined a owl:NamedIndividual , logic:GoalEvaluationStatus .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "logic:GoalEvaluationUndetermined MUST be a logic:GoalEvaluationStatus member: the value the teleology evaluator emits for a maintenance/avoidance/deadline goal whose bounding window is still open and for a deontic evaluation with no accessible ideal world — never silently read as Satisfied or as a vacuous obligation." .


# --- 32. Transaction-layer branching, concurrent, iterative, and fallback combinators exist (MUST) ---
ex:saTransactionCombinatorsFull a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/>
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
ASK {
    logic:Choice               a owl:Class .
    logic:ConcurrentComposition a owl:Class .
    logic:Iteration            a owl:Class .
    logic:Fallback             a owl:Class .
    logic:iterationBody        a owl:ObjectProperty .
    logic:iterationCondition   a owl:ObjectProperty .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "The four missing transaction-layer program combinators MUST exist: logic:Choice (guarded branching), logic:ConcurrentComposition (interleaved-path composition, distinct from the concurrency correctness concerns), logic:Iteration (loop with body + condition), and logic:Fallback (try primary, on failure alternate). Each is a boxTBox owl:Class mirroring logic:SerialConjunction. logic:iterationBody and logic:iterationCondition are the two dedicated properties of logic:Iteration (binary left/right operands do not fit a loop); the other three combinators reuse logic:leftOperand and logic:rightOperand." .

# --- 33. Transaction-layer combinators carry correct boxTBox graphBoxRole (MUST) ---
ex:saCombinatorBoxRole a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/>
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
ASK {
    logic:Choice                a owl:Class ; gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .
    logic:ConcurrentComposition a owl:Class ; gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .
    logic:Iteration             a owl:Class ; gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .
    logic:Fallback              a owl:Class ; gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "The four new program combinators (Choice, ConcurrentComposition, Iteration, Fallback) MUST carry gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox — they are program-combinator classes in the TBox, typed apart from formula connectives, mirroring the boxTBox role of logic:SerialConjunction." .

# --- 34. ConcurrentComposition is distinct from the concurrency correctness concerns (MUST-NOT) ---
ex:saConcurrentCompositionDistinct a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:mustNot ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/>
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
ASK {
    logic:ConcurrentComposition rdfs:subClassOf logic:SerializabilityCriterion .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "logic:ConcurrentComposition MUST NOT be a subclass of logic:SerializabilityCriterion (or any of the three concurrency correctness concerns): it is the COMPOSITION OPERATOR, while SerializabilityCriterion is a correctness PROPERTY OF A HISTORY — the three concurrency concerns are kept pairwise distinct precisely because they are not interchangeable." .

# === Semantics-aware validator findings + scoped coherence certificate ========
# The slice carries its own correctness claims for the coherence-certificate vocabulary as ontology
# data: the 8-way finding taxonomy, the two completeness-gated coherence artifacts,
# and the payload that scopes them. The runtime gate (conclusive->Certificate,
# bounded->Attestation, forbidden glut->refused) is authored canonically in Rust
# (crates/logic/src/certificate.rs); these assertions pin the vocabulary surface it
# projects from.
#
# OBSERVABILITY BOUNDARY (LOGIC-CONFORMANCE.md §"Tests as ontology data",
# §"The coherence certificate"). The coherence claim has two halves, and only one is
# checkable as ontology data through the conformance harness:
#
#   * OBSERVABLE — the REASONING VERDICT. "A within-world contradiction emits a
#     captured witness; the same contradiction isolated across worlds does not
#     contaminate either world." This IS checked behaviorally as ontology data by the
#     paraconsistency corpus, which the native engine genuinely evaluates and the
#     harness diffs against per-world expected/verdicts.json goldens:
#       - conformance/logic/cases/paraconsistency/within-world-glut/         => `inconsistent`
#         (the glut is captured + surfaced, i.e. DISCLOSED, not silently swallowed);
#       - conformance/logic/cases/paraconsistency/within-world-glut-isolated/ => `consistent`
#         (the SAME contradictory pair, split across two worlds, stays isolated);
#       - conformance/logic/cases/paraconsistency/cross-world-isolation/      => `consistent`
#         (cross-world coexistence, the original isolation witness).
#     These are GENUINELY-EVALUATED witnesses (verdict_mode=consistency runs
#     gmeow_logic::reason::dl_consistency, folding from the same closure as reason_all),
#     NOT term-existence probes.
#
#   * RUST-ONLY — the PERMITTED-vs-FORBIDDEN CLASSIFICATION of a disclosed glut, and the
#     certificate-vs-attestation completeness gate. Whether a captured within-world glut
#     is a permitted, disclosed conflict (coherent under a glut-admitting contract:
#     AdmitAllFour / ForbidGap) or a forbidden integrity violation (under a glut-forbidding
#     contract: ForbidGlut / ForbidGapAndGlut) is computed in Rust off the ReasoningResult
#     by the contract's ContradictionPolicy
#     (crates/logic/src/certificate.rs::CoherenceOutcome::from_reasoning_result, partitioning
#     purely on contradiction_policy.glut_permitted()). This classification is NOT folded
#     into the reasoned/materialized graph, and the conformance profile surface is closed
#     (reasoning_contract carries only `preset`, no admissible_valuation facet —
#     crates/conformance/src/profile.rs), so the harness CANNOT evaluate it as ontology data.
#     It is pinned canonically by the Rust certificate tests
#     (permitted_glut_is_coherent / forbidden_glut_refuses_and_issues_no_certificate /
#     bounded_forbidden_glut_attests_and_discloses_the_forbidden_witness). Cells 36-39 below
#     therefore pin only the vocabulary SURFACE of this Rust-checked classification (the two
#     completeness-gated artifacts, the permitted/=/forbidden distinctness, the four policy
#     valuations) — they do not, and honestly cannot, re-prove the classification behaviorally.

# --- 35. FindingCategory is a closed eight-member value set (MUST) ------------
ex:saFindingCategoryClosedValueSet a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/>
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
ASK {
    logic:FindingCategory a owl:Class ; gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .
    logic:FindingDataShapeViolation         a logic:FindingCategory .
    logic:FindingModelingDisciplineViolation a logic:FindingCategory .
    logic:FindingContradictionWitness       a logic:FindingCategory .
    logic:FindingPermittedEpistemicConflict a logic:FindingCategory .
    logic:FindingUnsupportedSemanticFeature a logic:FindingCategory .
    logic:FindingIncompleteCheck            a logic:FindingCategory .
    logic:FindingProjectionLoss             a logic:FindingCategory .
    logic:FindingPolicyWarning              a logic:FindingCategory .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "logic:FindingCategory MUST be a closed value class with exactly its eight named individuals -- the orthogonal-to-severity KIND axis that makes 'not all findings are failures' machine-checkable. The Rust gmeow_diagnostics::FindingCategory enum mirrors this set one-to-one." .

# --- 36. The two completeness-gated coherence artifacts exist (MUST) ----------
ex:saCoherenceArtifactsExist a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/>
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
ASK {
    logic:CoherenceCertificate      a owl:Class ; gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .
    logic:CoherenceCheckAttestation a owl:Class ; gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "Both coherence outcomes MUST exist as TBox classes: logic:CoherenceCertificate (issued ONLY from a conclusive check) and the strictly weaker logic:CoherenceCheckAttestation (a bounded/incomplete check). The completeness gate that chooses between them is the whole point of having two artifacts rather than one." .

# --- 37. Permitted conflict is distinct from a forbidden contradiction (MUST-NOT) ---
ex:saPermittedConflictNotContradictionWitness a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:mustNot ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/>
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
ASK {
    logic:FindingPermittedEpistemicConflict owl:sameAs logic:FindingContradictionWitness .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "The permitted, disclosed conflict MUST NOT be identified with the forbidden contradiction witness -- they are distinct logic:FindingCategory individuals. This is the load-bearing distinction: a glut under a glut-admitting contract is coherent (non-failing), a glut under a glut-forbidding one is an integrity violation; collapsing them would erase the central coherence-certificate claim." .

# --- 38. The scoped coherence payload properties exist (MUST) -----------------
ex:saCoherencePayloadPropertiesExist a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/>
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
ASK {
    logic:summarizesResult          a owl:ObjectProperty .
    logic:bundleHash                a owl:DatatypeProperty .
    logic:axiomHash                 a owl:DatatypeProperty .
    logic:contradictionPolicy       a owl:ObjectProperty .
    logic:checkIssuedAt             a owl:DatatypeProperty .
    logic:permittedConflictWitness  a owl:ObjectProperty .
    logic:forbiddenViolationWitness a owl:ObjectProperty .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "The scoped-payload properties MUST exist so a coherence outcome can carry its full evidence: the summarized result, the bundle/axiom hashes (H), the classifying contradiction policy, the injected issue timestamp, and the permitted/forbidden witness partition. Contract (C), fragment (F) and budget (B) are reached through logic:summarizesResult on the linked logic:ReasoningResult." .

# --- 39. contradictionPolicy ranges over the four admissible valuations (MUST) ---
ex:saContradictionPolicyValuesExist a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/>
ASK {
    logic:AdmitAllFour     a logic:AdmissibleValuationPolicy .
    logic:ForbidGap        a logic:AdmissibleValuationPolicy .
    logic:ForbidGlut       a logic:AdmissibleValuationPolicy .
    logic:ForbidGapAndGlut a logic:AdmissibleValuationPolicy .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "All four logic:AdmissibleValuationPolicy individuals MUST exist: logic:contradictionPolicy ranges over them, and the glut-admitting pair (AdmitAllFour, ForbidGap) versus the glut-forbidding pair (ForbidGlut, ForbidGapAndGlut) is exactly what classifies a witnessed glut as a permitted conflict or a forbidden violation. The Rust gmeow_logic_compile::compat::ContradictionPolicy enum mirrors these four and is wildcard-free so a new valuation is a compile error." .
